 "result": "Three tests fail for reasons other than the `partitioned` kwarg (from the subagent's report):\n\n1. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: `asgiref` isn't installed (the `async` extra), so `src/tessel/app.py:1090-1096` raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra`.\n\n2. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: it expects `max_form_memory_size` to default to `500_000`. Werkzeug 3.0.3 defaults to `None`, and `src/tessel/wrappers.py:110-111` just passes that through. This is also an old-Werkzeug problem, but it's a different missing feature than `partitioned`.\n\n3. **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: it fails only in the full run and passes alone. The subagent's best guess is that an unclosed `stream_with_context` generator from `test_stream_keeps_session` triggers an unraisable-exception failure here. That would make it indirect fallout of the main cause, but it's unconfirmed: the exact error message wasn't captured.\n\nCounting the first two as clearly separate, 22 of the 24 fail from the main cause directly or via the teardown/leak chain. The third is probably downstream of it.",
